00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.030 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hey there everyone it is i monster maze  normally i'm not the one to do topical  videos but hey it's breath of the wild  too we gotta talk about this news about  this game is few and far between so i  might as well give my two cents on the  matter this will be one of those rare  times where i'm completely off script i  haven't written anything down so please  bear with me and forgive me for all the  stumbling so nintendo put up a new video  about the development stage of brevtuatu  and first of all adrian numa my man  looking good with his new hairdo i guess  quarantine is officially over in japan  so yeah the game has officially been  delayed to 2023. now to be honest as the  optimist that i am this was not in my  line of expectations i mean i didn't  rule out the possibility but since they  announced the release here only about  nine months ago i thought they were  pretty confident that they were gonna  make it but well apparently not on the  one hand this is kinda disappointing  obviously having to wait longer is never  fun but at the same time i think it  would benefit the game to be honest 2022  is so incredibly packed we got horizon  forbidden west alden ring kirby god of  war is on the way xenoblade chronicles 3  star field hogwarts legacy which by the  way looks amazing has been announced for  december and i'm pretty sure i'm  forgetting even more especially with a  game like elden ring which took the  world by storm and is already being  compared to breath the wild in many ways  i think this is a good opportunity to  give breath to altoo some room to  breathe now i'm not gonna speculate  whether or not this means the game will  be released with new hardware i mean i  hate talking about switch pro and rumors  like that i mean who the heck knows at  this point you know so instead let's  focus on what we do know from the  announcement itself first of all notice  how onuma says that the game will not  just take place on the surface but also  in the skies above which we already knew  from the second teaser however that the  expanded world goes beyond that which is  great news a lot of people were kind of  worried about the surface of hyrule  being revisited including me because  well we already explored this world  extensively and justifyingly so there  were doubts if the sky was going to be  enough to make the game feel fresh and  new and not just a glorified dlc so to  speak and well the man himself agra  seems to put our hearts at ease and  there will be more than just a familiar  surface and the sky what exactly this  expanded world entails of course we  don't know right now the usual stuff  comes to mind like a new province new  islands underground underwater things  which have been theorized before but to  get actual confirmation that there will  be more is again absolutely great news  and to top it off aunuma states that  there will be even more gameplay  elements more encounters and an even  wider variety of features he really  seems to hammer home the fact that this  will be a very different experience and  finally let's go over the new footage  because despite the disappointing  announcement they actually did show some  new stuff not a whole lot but hey it's  something this entire sequence although  brief only lasting a few seconds does at  least confirm two things number one  link's face is just fine no scars or  deformities no malice eyes big hand  everybody he's okay i guess that theory  goes out the window  and two he still has the master sword  it's just that well it's not exactly in  great shape so the whole idea that the  sword fell into the chasm and maybe  zelda has it that goes out the window  too this basically confirms that the  attack on link's arm by malice was  indeed ganondorf going after the master  sword and for good reason it's like the  one thing capable of inflicting mortal  damage to him so that is a sweet power  move by g-man over here it also suggests  that the game will likely revolve around  restoring the master sword as without it  link won't even be able to hurt  ganondorf or at least not kill him of  course this would also mean that the  game cannot be beaten like breath of the  wild where you could just go straight to  calamity ganon and kick his ass that's  not gonna work if you don't have the  tools to do it this could suggest that  the game will have a more linear  approach of course the restoration of  the master sword could still be done out  of order in fact i'm expecting that you  probably can but it won't be as easy as  just walking up to the castle i'm  definitely considering making a more  comprehensive theory about this because  i have a lot of ideas but for now i'll  just say that it's becoming more and  more likely that the sky islands are  indeed tied to the triforce or the  sacred realm in some way we know from  previous games that the master sword's  power to repel evil is something sacred  something tied to sages and the gods and  so on in breath of the wild however  there were no sages at least not in the  traditional sense we only had the four  champions but that's not really the same  thing sages have some sort of special  connection to the gods and as we saw in  the wind waker they can pray to the gods  to restore the master sword's power the  closest thing we saw in breath of the  wild were the sheikah monks at the end  of the trial of the sword which did  indeed restore the sacred glow to the  blade but after they did their bodies  disappeared and their spirits seemed to  have moved on to the afterlife so that  doesn't seem to be an option anymore the  only other entity we saw capable of  restoring the master sword was the deku  tree who is set to tap into some sort of  sacred energy to fix the blade and lo  and behold as many have pointed out the  deku tree seems to be gone in breath the  wall too he's no longer where he should  be so it really seems like ganondorf  tried to eliminate every option to fix  the sword again for good reason lastly i  will quickly touch upon two more things  first is this yellow flame hovering in  front of link i'm not entirely sure but  i get the impression that it's talking  to him the way link has his arm out and  staring right at it and then turning  around to grab the master sword  definitely suggests as much and if it is  indeed sentient the most logical  conclusion is that it's probably the  spirit of whoever this hand belonged to  you know the one that was clutching onto  ganondorf's body which could mean that  we're looking at a new companion  character someone who knows how to  restore the master sword and guides link  on his way who this character is we  don't know of course maybe it's a past  hero or an ancient sage of some kind  we'll just have to wait and see you are  more than welcome to share your  suggestions lastly we do see that link  has some sort of symbol on his hand and  this is definitely not the triforce  instead it's probably tied to the race  or tribe this being belongs to my  current take is that after the attack on  the master sword and link's arm link  will go unconscious which will no doubt  also serve as the excuse to start with  three hearts again and the new footage  likely takes place close to just after  he wakes up when he first realizes what  happened and the spirit inside his arm  will explain how to fix it in fact on  the floor we can see a circular design  with symbols on it very similar to this  shot where link is seemingly half naked  and unconscious and the spirit possesses  his arm and here too we see the same  type of symbols on the floor obviously  in this shot it's almost completely dark  so probably on the ground so my best  guess at this point is that maybe this  entire platform he's laying on will rise  into the sky which would explain how he  gets to the sky for the first time and  that is all i have to say about it at  least for now again don't hesitate to  share your thoughts in the comments  below i'd love to hear what you guys  have to say this is dawn signing off and  have a good one

